
//
// This file specifies how Exemplar enhancements are handicapped.
//
// There is an entry in both fields for each level. (So, there should be
// 50 of them.)

// Clamp attribmod magnitudes to this value before even checking for exceeding
//   the Limits.
PreClamp .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, .4167, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000

// If the magnitude of an attribmod is larger or equal to value found in
//   limits (looking at the Exemplar's combat level), then the handicap is 
//   applied.
Limits 0.05, 0.05, 0.05, 0.05, 0.05, 0.05, 0.05, 0.05, 0.05, 0.05, 0.10, 0.10, 0.10, 0.10, 0.10, 0.10, 0.10, 0.10, 0.10, 0.10, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20

// The weights specify the handicap. The handicap is the weight at the
//   exemplar's experience level divided by the weight at the exemplar's
//   current combat level.
Weights 0.022, 0.045, 0.068, 0.092, 0.116, 0.141, 0.166, 0.192, 0.219, 0.246, 0.274, 0.302, 0.331, 0.361, 0.391, 0.422, 0.454, 0.486, 0.519, 0.553, 0.587, 0.623, 0.659, 0.696, 0.733, 0.772, 0.811, 0.852, 0.893, 0.935, 0.978, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000

// Clamp attribmod magnitudes to this value after doing the weighting.
PostClamp 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000, 1.000

